{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce a modern Net Book Agreement to allow fixed retail prices on new books",
        "additional_details": "Independent bookshops are an important part of our high streets, communities and literary culture. However, they face increasing challenges when competing with large online retailers and national chains that can offer substantial discounts on newly published books.\r\n \r\nWe believe the original Net Book Agreement helped create a more level playing field by limiting discounting and allowing bookshops to better compete through their service, knowledge and customer experience rather than price alone.",
        "background": "We ask the Government to review current competition legislation and create a modern equivalent of the Net Book Agreement. Allow publishers to set fixed retail prices for books that all sellers must follow for a limited period after publication. We believe it would help protect independent bookshops.",
